An installed region does not name its process.
Clearing it would leave the process's PMP image as it was, the region a mere capability;
an installed region names its process.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: installed region does not name its process
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -110,7 +110,6 @@ int process_install(struct process *proc, unsigned slot,
     }
 
     proc->slots[slot] = cap_to_frame(base, size, rights);
-    proc->slots[slot].b = held_word(v2p(proc), 0);
     cap_attach(parent, &proc->slots[slot]);
     rebuild_pmp(proc);
     return KERR_OK;
